// Issue #229 follow-up: `name : type` in a variant field is a *label* on a
// field of type `type` (see docs/ta-language-spec.md「ADT」). The type after
// the ':' is what the declaration carries, so passing a string where `int`
// is declared is a type error.
//
// Before the parser fix the variant-arg path (expression call args) split
// `num : int` into three fields (num, nil, int); resolve_field_type
// manufactured the malformed type ('app nil) from the nil field, so the
// declared field types were garbage and wrong-typed arguments unified
// silently. Issue #208 fixed only the crash when that malformed type was
// formatted (the guard in fmt_type_name stays as a defensive net); this file
// now pins the real thing — the annotation is the field's type.
pub type Rational { R(num : int, den : int) }

pub fn f(x : int) -> Rational { R(x, "oops") }

fn main() -> int { 0 }

// expect: cannot unify string with int